+/* PW64: the present tick (docs/notes/framerate.md "Present tick"): the OS
+ * core posts PW64_PRESENT_MSG at the display rate and the VI latches the
+ * pending swap there instead of at the retrace. This handler only sets
+ * pw64_sc_present and re-enters _uvScHandleRetrace, which shares its swap
+ * flip, cmdQ drain and RSP-idle gfx start with the retrace path while the
+ * clock update, RSP/RDP timeouts, audio-busy gate, audio start, yield
+ * handling and client notification stay retrace-only: no decomp statement
+ * is restated here (the release ships only our added lines as ops,
+ * first-run-build.md T16). The shared drain logs with the retrace's labels
+ * (also for an unknown task type at a tick: unreachable, only gfx and
+ * audio tasks are queued). An audio task taken at the tick is only stored;
+ * the next retrace starts it, exactly as before (it would have waited in
+ * cmdQ until then). A gfx task may start while one waits: the HLE finishes
+ * it before the next retrace is delivered (OS-core invariant,
+ * native-build.md §8), so that retrace finds the RSP idle and starts the
+ * audio task directly, never the yield path (D_802B9C6B). While audio runs
+ * (RSP 'a', e.g. retrace and tick delivered together), _uvScDoneAud starts
+ * the flipped-in task, as after a retrace. */
+static void _uvScHandlePresent(void) {
+    pw64_sc_present = 1;
+    _uvScHandleRetrace();
+    pw64_sc_present = 0;
+}
